## 📊 Mapping Status Code Symptoms to Vulnerabilities
When running your automated pipeline framework tool, watching the status codes shift tells you exactly what layer of the application structure your payload has interacted with:

| Status Code Shift | Primary Diagnostic Meaning | Potential Vulnerability Hint |
|---|---|---|
| 200 OK ──► 500 Internal Error | Your input broke a backend code script or query syntax structure. | SQL Injection, RCE, XML Parsing Error |
| 403 Forbidden ──► 200 OK | An input bypassed a web tracking routing restriction rule. | Broken Authentication, Proxy Bypasses |
| 200 OK ──► 404 Not Found | The application evaluated your input and redirected to a dead route folder. | Path Traversal, Client-Side Routing bugs |
| 200 OK ──► Hangs Forever / Timeout | Your input caused the OS kernel to freeze or loop indefinitely. | Blind RCE, ReDoS (Regular Expression DoS) |

